# Cloudflare Pages deployment routing
#
# SPA mode: no top-level /404.html — Pages serves /index.html for unknown
# *client routes* (e.g. /login, /explore). Do NOT add a root 404.html unless
# you also restore SPA via a carefully ordered /* → /index.html 200 rule.
#
# Hashed Vite assets live under /assets/. Missing files there must NOT fall
# through to index.html (that returns 200 text/html and breaks module scripts:
# "Expected JavaScript module but server returned text/html").
#
# Fix: public/assets/404.html (and brand/404.html) — Cloudflare serves the
# closest 404.html for missing paths under that directory while SPA mode stays on.
#
# Existing static files always win over 404 pages:
#   /assets/*.js|*.css|*.map
#   /*.js /*.css /*.map /*.png /*.webp /*.svg
#   /brand/*
